  "comments": [
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ca2c8198_6ae714dd",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/ffa.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 329,
      "author": {
        "id": 1951687
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-07-15T14:29:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hum, it is a bit convoluted to have both \"is_lend\" and a static branch here, in a such low-level function.\n\nNow the mechanism for the share/unshare donate/reclaim is the same, perhaps it\u0027d be better to use a function pointer as an argument directly, and let do_ffa_mem_xfer() choose which one is best?\n\nPerhaps then a renaming lend/reclaim instead of share/unshare would be more appropriate?",
      "revId": "774a3804f96edca34f8108818174ec025979350a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "59fd2554_d53cb08a",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/ffa.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 401,
      "author": {
        "id": 1942270
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-05-08T11:33:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is a problem if fragmentation API is used in conjunction with LEND because the sub-sequent fragment will be shared (thus the memory that they cover will not be unmapped from host stage-2).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 401,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 401,
        "endChar": 22
      },
      "revId": "774a3804f96edca34f8108818174ec025979350a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1274f146_70d9de26",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/mem_protect.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 2438,
      "author": {
        "id": 1951687
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-07-15T14:29:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "host_reclaim_ffa ?\n\nAlso why the need to know it was lent? The caller should know",
      "revId": "774a3804f96edca34f8108818174ec025979350a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0dc3986d_0cb59fc7",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/mem_protect.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 2438,
      "author": {
        "id": 1942270
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-07-15T14:34:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The caller doesn\u0027t know for `ffa_host_unshare_ranges` unless you keep all the handles for every transaction which I want to avoid.",
      "parentUuid": "1274f146_70d9de26",
      "revId": "774a3804f96edca34f8108818174ec025979350a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8442cafc_0571cb07",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/mem_protect.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 2438,
      "author": {
        "id": 1951687
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-07-15T14:39:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is it because the same FF-A \"RECLAIM\" invocation would be used in both sharing and lend case?\n\nIf that\u0027s the case, how about\n\n1. try to unshare (will walk the stage-2 page-table and would abort if the memory is not owned by the host)\n2. on failure, try to \"reclaim\"",
      "parentUuid": "0dc3986d_0cb59fc7",
      "revId": "774a3804f96edca34f8108818174ec025979350a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1b64d4dd_bab9b3e2",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/mem_protect.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 2438,
      "author": {
        "id": 1942270
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-07-15T14:50:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think you need to walk the stage-2 pagetables. You just need to look into the vmemmap to see the page state and if it\u0027s NO_PAGE you know that is was a lend.",
      "parentUuid": "8442cafc_0571cb07",
      "revId": "774a3804f96edca34f8108818174ec025979350a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5c607b31_6b93fe72",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/mem_protect.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 2438,
      "author": {
        "id": 1951687
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-07-15T15:15:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Then you\u0027d probably need to restrict the donate_ffa and share_ffa to !MMIO regions to avoid this imbalance.\n\nAlternatively, __host_check_page_state_range() will cover all cases.",
      "parentUuid": "1b64d4dd_bab9b3e2",
      "revId": "774a3804f96edca34f8108818174ec025979350a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b30fbaae_79d48d89",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/mem_protect.c",
